  2): Abstract describes breast cancer sentinel node biopsy, not pancreatic lesions\n2. Review articles/pictorial       
  essays (Studies 37, 58, 63): No original diagnostic accuracy data\n3. Treatment study (Study 72): Preoperative        
  biliary drainage trial, not diagnostic accuracy\n4. Truncated abstracts (Studies 26, 53, 85): Insufficient            
  information to assess eligibility\n5. Editorials/commentaries (Studies 71, 95): No primary data\n6. Inadequate        
  reference standard (Study 13): Results based on radiologic findings only\n\n**Included Studies:** All 89 included     
  studies report diagnostic accuracy data for imaging modalities (CT, MRI, PET, EUS, EUS-FNA, EUS elastography) or      
  biomarker testing in pancreatic lesions with appropriate reference standards (histopathology, surgical excision, or   
  clinical follow-up ≥6 months).",                                                                                      
