reference standard (1).', 'task_outcome_detailed': 'Title/abstract screening completed for studies 1-100 from the 
systematic review on imaging modalities for characterising focal pancreatic lesions. \n\n**Summary Statistics:**\n- 
Total studies screened: 100\n- Included: 89 (89%)\n- Excluded: 11 (11%)\n\n**Exclusion Categories:**\n1. Wrong 
population (Study 2): Abstract describes breast cancer sentinel node biopsy, not pancreatic lesions\n2. Review 
articles/pictorial essays (Studies 37, 58, 63): No original diagnostic accuracy data\n3. Treatment study (Study 72): 
Preoperative biliary drainage trial, not diagnostic accuracy\n4. Truncated abstracts (Studies 26, 53, 85): Insufficient 
information to assess eligibility\n5. Editorials/commentaries (Studies 71, 95): No primary data\n6. Inadequate reference
standard (Study 13): Results based on radiologic findings only\n\n**Included Studies:** All 89 included studies report 
diagnostic accuracy data for imaging modalities (CT, MRI, PET, EUS, EUS-FNA, EUS elastography) or biomarker testing in 
pancreatic lesions with appropriate reference standards (histopathology, surgical excision, or clinical follow-up ≥6 
months).', 'additional_context': 'The screening followed a conservative approach, including studies when uncertain. Most
