│ fine needle aspiration biopsy (EUS-FNA) is a recent innovation in the evaluation of gastrointestinal and pulmonary   │
│ malignancies. AIMS To review the experience with EUS-FNA of a large single centre. METHODS 333 consecutive patients  │
│ underwent EUS-FNA. Follow up data were available on 327 lesions in 317 patients, including 160 lymph nodes, 144      │
