  ### 3. Additional context (if relevant):                                                                              
  - **Inclusion Criteria Applied**: Studies were included if they evaluated the diagnostic accuracy of specified        
  imaging modalities (CT, MRI, PET, EUS, EUS elastography, EUS-FNA/biopsy) for focal pancreatic lesions against a       
  valid reference standard (histopathology from surgical excision, or biopsy + ≥6 months clinical follow-up).           
  - **Exclusion Reasons**: 18 studies were excluded primarily for being commentaries/letters to the editor (622, 633,   
  668, 684), systematic reviews (623), focusing on clinical signs/symptoms rather than imaging/biopsy (613),            
  evaluating operator training rather than modality accuracy (642), mismatched abstracts/titles (646, 692), or          
  focusing on non-pancreatic lesions (654). Study 609 was excluded for using ERCP as the reference standard instead of  
  histopathology/follow-up. Study 676 was excluded due to lack of a surgical standard in all cases.                     
  - **Conservative Approach**: Studies with borderline reference standards or combined modalities were generally        
  included to avoid missing potentially relevant data for the review.                                                   
  """                                                                                                                   
  final_answer(final_answer_variable)                                                                                   
